GDDL License v1.0

Intent:
This license allows anyone to freely use, modify, redistribute, and embed
GDDL in other software, including commercial software, while preventing
GDDL itself from being sold as a competing software product.

Copyright (c) 2026 Sami Koistinen


You may:

- Use GDDL for any purpose, free of charge.
- Read, modify, and share the source code.
- Use modified versions privately or within any organization.
- Redistribute the original or modified GDDL software and source code free
  of charge, provided this license and all copyright notices are kept intact.
- Include GDDL, with or without modifications, in your own software,
  including commercial software.
- Charge for services such as installation, customization, support,
  consulting, or training.


You may not:

- Sell or license GDDL, its source code, or a modified version of GDDL as a
  standalone software product.
- Claim GDDL as your own.
- Remove or alter this license or the copyright notices.


Competing Product Clarification:

For purposes of the restriction above, a product or service counts as "a
modified version of GDDL" if its value derives, entirely or substantially,
from GDDL's own functionality — regardless of renaming, rebranding, or the
extent of source code changes made to it. This clarification exists
specifically so the restriction above cannot be avoided through modification
or renaming alone.

This clarification does not extend the restriction to your own software
merely because it includes, depends on, or is built using GDDL — see
"Included Software" below, which remains freely allowed. Nor does it limit
charging for services such as installation, customization, support,
consulting, or training, as already stated above.


Included Software:

If your software includes GDDL or a modified version of GDDL, you must:

- Identify GDDL by name in your documentation or other accompanying materials.
- Include this license.
- State that GDDL is licensed separately under the GDDL License v1.0.


Patent Grant:

The copyright holder grants you a worldwide, royalty-free license to any
patents owned by the copyright holder that are required to use, modify, or
distribute GDDL under this license.

This grant applies only to patents covering GDDL itself and does not apply
to unrelated inventions or technologies.


Examples:

The following examples are intended to clarify how this license applies.


Allowed:

- A person downloads GDDL, modifies it, and uses their modified version to
  create their own game.

- A game developer embeds GDDL into their game so players can create and
  load mods.

- A company modifies GDDL internally to better fit their development
  workflow.

- A company ships a commercial game that includes GDDL or a modified version
  of GDDL.

- A website, package manager, or code hosting service provides a free mirror
  of the GDDL source code.

- A developer creates tutorials, integrations, plugins, or services that use
  GDDL.

- A consultant charges for installing, customizing, or supporting GDDL.


Not Allowed:

- A company takes GDDL, renames it, and sells it as their own compiler or
  development tool.

- A company sells a modified version of GDDL as a separate product.

- A person sells copies of the GDDL source code.

- A person removes the GDDL copyright notices or license and distributes it
  as their own work.

- A company creates a paid download where the main product being sold is
  access to GDDL itself.


These examples do not replace the license terms. If an example conflicts
with the license text, the license text takes precedence.


